      "note": "the cap a hundred times higher: a packet that claims more than 100 MB is allocated"
    },
    {
      "id": "S3",
      "file": "src/core/src/ch10setup.cpp",
      "old": "    if (required > static_cast<std::size_t>(PCMConstants::kMaxPacketBufferSize))\n",
      "new": "    if (required >= static_cast<std::size_t>(PCMConstants::kMaxPacketBufferSize))\n",
      "expect": "survived",
      "note": "the boundary itself: a packet of exactly 100 MB is not tried, because it would be allocated and read for the test"
    },
    {
      "id": "S4",
      "file": "src/core/src/ch10setup.cpp",
      "old": "    if (buffer.size() < required)\n",
      "new": "    if (buffer.size() > required)\n",
      "expect": "caught",
      "note": "the buffer never grows to the packet: the read is refused as too small"
    },
    {
